\title{comdynamite: Process-Based Metacommunity Simulations with Phylogenetic Structure}
\description{
Simulates metacommunity dynamics with the process-based model of Thompson et al. (2020) \doi{10.1111/ele.13568}: density-independent growth that depends on the match between each species' environmental optimum and the local environment, Beverton-Holt competition, Poisson demographic stochasticity, and emigration and immigration among sites. Landscapes can be spatially implicit, with uniform dispersal, or explicit grids with an exponential dispersal kernel and a spatially autocorrelated environment, and the environment can change over time. Species traits (environmental optima, niche breadths and maximum growth rates) can carry phylogenetic signal, and interspecific competition can be structured by relatedness. The model was implemented from the published equations.
